#
# w5server.conf.tmpl — W5Server (control-plane) config (TEMPLATE)
#
# Rendered by docker/entrypoint.sh (whitelist envsubst) into
# /etc/w5base/w5server.conf, then read by: sbin/W5Server -c w5server.
# W5Server is the persistent TCP process server the web frontend depends on.
#
# Pulls DB credentials from the shared databases.conf fragment via INCLUDE.
# Two values are substituted from the environment at render time:
#   - W5BASESRVUSER          the service account W5Server runs as (defaults w5base)
#   - W5BASE_OPERATION_MODE  the operation mode (see W5BaseOperationMode below)
# All other values are literals mirroring etc/w5base/default.conf, EXCEPT
# W5ServerPort, which prefixes the bare port with the IPv4 loopback bind host
# (see the detailed note above the W5ServerPort directive below).
#
# WHY W5BaseOperationMode is rendered HERE (rather than left to inherit
# etc/w5base/default.conf): the operation mode MUST be IDENTICAL for the control
# plane (W5Server) and the web frontend (w5base.conf). default.conf ships
# "online", so if this template omitted the mode, W5Server would silently
# inherit "online" while the frontend ran ${W5BASE_OPERATION_MODE} — a
# divergence W5Base forbids (README.txt). Rendering the SAME env value into both
# configs (w5server.conf here and w5base.conf) keeps them in lock-step.
#
INCLUDE /etc/w5base/databases.conf
#
# W5ServerPort — the address:port the control plane LISTENS on. It is
# deliberately prefixed with the IPv4 loopback host (127.0.0.1:) instead of the
# bare "12833" that etc/w5base/default.conf ships:
#   sbin/W5Server passes this value straight to Net::Server as its `port`, and
#   Net::Server's default host ("*") resolves to the IPv6 wildcard "::". Docker
#   containers in this environment have NO IPv6 address on loopback, so a "::"
#   bind fails with "[Invalid argument]" (Net/Server/Proto/TCP.pm) and W5Server
#   dies on startup — 12833 never opens and the web frontend then reports
#   "W5Server is not available". Pinning the bind to the IPv4 loopback forces a
#   working listen socket and is consistent with W5ServerAllow="127.0.0.1"
#   below (W5Server and Apache share this container, so loopback is the only
#   address the frontend needs to reach it). The port is unchanged (12833).
#
# This is the SERVER bind ONLY. The client side (bin/app.pl under Apache, via
# the w5base config) reads W5ServerHost and W5ServerPort SEPARATELY and is
# UNAFFECTED: w5base.conf sets no W5ServerPort, so it inherits the bare "12833"
# and W5ServerHost="localhost" from etc/w5base/default.conf, and connects to
# 127.0.0.1:12833 — exactly what this server binds.
W5ServerPort="127.0.0.1:12833"
W5ServerUser="${W5BASESRVUSER}"
W5ServerGroup="daemon"
W5ServerState="/var/opt/w5base/state"
W5ServerAllow="127.0.0.1"
W5BaseOperationMode="${W5BASE_OPERATION_MODE}"
